<title>ITALY: Minimum rate 7.51 pct at Italy BOT buyback.</title>
<headline>Minimum rate 7.51 pct at Italy BOT buyback.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The minimum rate at today's 2.5 trillion lire buyback of short-term Treasury bills (BOTs) by the Bank of Italy was 7.51 percent compared with 8.04 percent previously, the Bank said.</p>
<p>The average rate was 7.64 percent against 8.10 percent at the previous operation also for 2.5 trillion lire on September 13.</p>
<p>The Bank said it received 20 bids of which 12 were met in full and one in part.</p>
